findings.body:
`TabDisplayView.scrollToTab` still builds `IndexPath(row: scrollState.toIndex, section: 1)`. Before this PR, section 1 was the tabs section. The data source now emits one section (`.tabs`, index 0), so every scroll request points at a section that does not exist.

The `isValid(indexPath:)` guard inside the `DispatchQueue.main.async` block will likely stop the call, so this is probably a silent no-op rather than a crash. Either way, the tab tray will no longer scroll to the selected tab or a newly added tab. The XCUITest identifier changes (`tabCell_1_1` to `tabCell_0_1`) show the tabs section is now 0, so the production code is the part that was missed.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Views/TabDisplayView.swift" lines="169-180"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The `scrollToTab` path has no unit test, which is why CI did not catch it. Add one that asserts the index path section after the collapse.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Views/TabDisplayView.swift" lines="172-172"}
let indexPath = IndexPath(row: scrollState.toIndex, section: 0)

When the user switches to a panel where no tab is selected, `createTabScrollBehavior` used to return `tabs.count - 1`, the last tab. This PR changes it to `state.tabs.count`, which is one past the last index.

The existing test `testCreateTabScrollBehavior_forScrollToSelectedTab_noSelectedTab_returnsLastTab_ifTabsNotEmpty` still asserts `tabCount - 1` and is not in the diff, so it will fail. The new value is also not a valid index into `state.tabs`. Even with the section fix above, scrolling to `count` would target nothing.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/State/TabsPanelState.swift" lines="139-144"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The comment above the line still says the goal is to scroll to the bottom of the panel, which is the last tab. Reverting to `count - 1` keeps that behavior and the test passing.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/State/TabsPanelState.swift" lines="143-143"}
return ScrollState(toIndex: state.tabs.count - 1, withAnimation: shouldAnimate)

The first three lines of `TabPanelAction.swift` (the MPL 2.0 header) are gone. Every other Swift file in this module starts with that header, and the removal looks accidental, since the PR only deletes the inactive-tab members from this file.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Tabs/Action/TabPanelAction.swift" lines="1-3"}

Restore the header so the file matches the rest of the module and passes any license-header lint check.

The four inactive-tab strings were moved from `TabsTray` into a new `struct v147` at the end of `Strings.swift` instead of being deleted. Nothing in the Swift code I could find references them after this PR. `TabsTrayInactiveTabsSectionTitle` and the `Settings.Tabs.CustomizeTabsSection.InactiveTabs*` strings also look unreferenced now. The `v147` name also doesn't match how the other sections in this file are named.

If the goal is removal, delete these definitions and the matching `.strings` keys in the localization files as part of this cleanup. Localization keys are usually pruned in a separate string-removal pass, so if that is the plan, say so in a comment.

